<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Highveld yr shr slides, div decreased.</title>
<headline>Highveld yr shr slides, div decreased.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     73.6	  vs	 218.6</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   68.7	  vs	 216.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 35.0	  vs	 90.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   69.45	 vs	 200.85</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   67.41	 vs	 261.43</p>
<p>    Tax received	     2.05	 vs	 60.59 paid</p>
<p>    Turnover	     2,705.31	 vs	 2,535.04</p>
<p>Full name: Highveld steel and Vanadium Corp Ltd (steel and allied)</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters forecast earnings per share ranging between 73.0 to 85.0 cents with consensus at 78.0 cents. The dividend was seen ranging between 32.0 to 40.0 cents from 90.0 cents.</p>
<p>The company said it would offer capitalisation shares in lieu of the cash dividend.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
